# Bear Your Soul (OSRS Wiki "Transcript:Bear Your Soul", with Aretha's and the Key Master's
# standard dialogue from "Transcript:Aretha" / "Transcript:Key Master"), via
# tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py, merged by hand. Lines marked (authored) are not Wiki.
0	section	Talking to Aretha before reading the book
1	line	Aretha	Respect the souls, traveller.
1	option	Why are all these souls here?
2	line	Player	Why are all these souls here?
2	line	Aretha	A corporeal body is a mere flesh-temple in which the soul dwells. As the body fails, the soul loses its home. Without guidance, it would drift into oblivion.
2	line	Aretha	However, the Soul Altar provides a beacon, drawing the souls to this place where they may join the River.
2	line	Aretha	The River leads the souls through unchartable realms, transcending the plane of the world as you see it, but the three-headed Guardian keeps them safe.
2	line	Aretha	The souls are the dead of Kourend - ensure you respect the souls.
2	action	other
1	option	Why are you here?
2	line	Player	Why are you here?
2	line	Aretha	I am here to salute the dead of Kourend whose souls are joining the River. Ensure you respect the souls.
2	action	other
1	option	Okay, I'm respecting the souls.
2	line	Player	Okay, I'm respecting the souls.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Aretha
1	line	Aretha	Respect the souls, traveller.
1	option	Why are all these souls here?
2	line	Player	Why are all these souls here?
2	line	Aretha	A corporeal body is a mere flesh-temple in which the soul dwells. As the body fails, the soul loses its home. Without guidance, it would drift into oblivion.
2	line	Aretha	However, the Soul Altar provides a beacon, drawing the souls to this place where they may join the River.
2	line	Aretha	The River leads the souls through unchartable realms, transcending the plane of the world as you see it, but the three-headed Guardian keeps them safe.
2	line	Aretha	The souls are the dead of Kourend - ensure you respect the souls.
2	action	other
1	option	Why are you here?
2	line	Player	Why are you here?
2	line	Aretha	I am here to salute the dead of Kourend whose souls are joining the River. Ensure you respect the souls.
2	action	other
1	option	I've been reading your book...
2	line	Player	I've been reading your book: 'The Journey of Souls'
2	line	Aretha	Let me guess, traveller... did you come to ask me where the soul bearer was buried? Every mortal who reads my book seems to want to get their hands on it.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Yes please.
3	line	Player	Yes please.
3	line	Aretha	Mortals are so predictable. This is the kind of thinking that led that adventurer to break into the Guardian's cave and damage the soul bearer in the first place.
3	line	Aretha	It occurs to me, though, that even if you dig it up, the artefact is damaged. Although the Elders of Arceuus never had the knowledge to repair it, there is one who may be able to help.
3	line	Aretha	I speak of the Key Master, he who watches over the cave of the three-headed Guardian of the River. He has been there for countless years, and will have absorbed power from the River in that time.
3	line	Aretha	Now, we buried the artefact in the crypt of the Arceuus church. As I have revealed this secret to you, you will no longer be affected by the spells that prevent unwary explorers from stumbling across it.
3	line	Player	Thanks! I'll be off now.
3	action	end
2	option	No, I don't want your smelly soul bearer.
3	line	Player	No, I don't want your smelly soul bearer.
3	line	Aretha	Hmmph! So what do you want? I trust you will respect the souls while you are in this hallowed place.
3	action	end
1	option	Okay, I'm respecting the souls.
2	line	Player	Okay, I'm respecting the souls.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Aretha after recovering the damaged soul bearer
1	line	Aretha	Respect the souls, traveller.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Why are all these souls here?
2	line	Player	Why are all these souls here?
2	line	Aretha	A corporeal body is a mere flesh-temple in which the soul dwells. As the body fails, the soul loses its home. Without guidance, it would drift into oblivion.
2	line	Aretha	However, the Soul Altar provides a beacon, drawing the souls to this place where they may join the River.
2	line	Aretha	The River leads the souls through unchartable realms, transcending the plane of the world as you see it, but the three-headed Guardian keeps them safe.
2	line	Aretha	The souls are the dead of Kourend - ensure you respect the souls.
2	action	other
1	option	Why are you here?
2	line	Player	Why are you here?
2	line	Aretha	I am here to salute the dead of Kourend whose souls are joining the River. Ensure you respect the souls.
2	action	other
1	option	About the soul bearer again...
2	line	Player	About the soul bearer again... I've dug it up, but it's damaged.
2	line	Aretha	This should be of no surprise to you, adventurer, if you paid attention to my book. Indeed, I even spoke of this matter when I first told you where the artefact was buried.
2	line	Aretha	Although the Elders of Arceuus never had the knowledge to repair it, I told you of one who may be able to help.
2	line	Aretha	I spoke of the Key Master, he who watches over the cave of the three-headed Guardian of the River. He has been there for countless years, and will have absorbed power from the River in that time.
2	line	Player	Oh yes, I see.
2	action	end
1	option	Okay, I'm respecting the souls.
2	line	Player	Okay, I'm respecting the souls.
2	action	end
