0	section	Talking to the Key Master
1	line	Player	Aretha said you might be able to repair the soul bearer for me.
1	line	Key Master	The soul bearer! You have the soul bearer! The voices speak of it often. It is from this place, yet it is not of this place.
1	line	Player	Will you repair it?
1	line	Key Master	The voices tell me I can. They speak to me!
1	box	The Key Master repairs your soul bearer.
1	line	Key Master	The voices say you must use it wisely.
1	option	What voices?
2	line	Player	What voices?
# (authored) The Wiki only says "above" for this option.
2	line	Key Master	The voices of the River! They whisper of the souls that pass by, day and night. They never stop...
2	action	above
1	option	Thanks, I will.
2	line	Player	Thanks, I will.
2	action	end
0	section	Key Master standard dialogue
1	line	Key Master	Who goes there? This is no place for a human. You need to leave.
1	line	Player	You're starting to scare me man...
1	line	Key Master	I am no man! They changed me and cursed me to remain here...
1	option	What do you mean they changed you?
2	line	Player	What do you mean they changed you?
2	line	Key Master	I was once a free man, powerful and wealthy. I owned several apothecaries across Kourend and sold the tastiest potions in the land.
2	line	Player	What happened?
2	line	Key Master	One of my greatest inventions, it was going so well. I spent days finding the right herbs, I travelled across all of Kourend to find the most exotic weeds. Once I had gathered them all, I put them in a potion and mixed in
2	line	Key Master	the final ingredient.
2	cond	If the player has not travelled to Great Kourend:
3	line	Player	Kourend? Interesting...
2	cond	If the player has travelled to Great Kourend:
3	line	Player	Kourend? Oh yeah, I've been there.
2	line	Key Master	Yes, yes... The potion tasted delicious but it was missing a tiny something so I added Magic roots to the potion. It started to pulsate and glow! I took a sip and I felt like a million gold! A few seconds later my eye sight
2	line	Key Master	began to blur, my brain was throbbing. I fell and hit my head on my worktop, then it all went black.
2	line	Player	Ouch! But, you still haven't said who changed you?
2	line	Key Master	Will you let me finish?
2	line	Key Master	I woke up screaming in pain. Blue foam streaming out of my mouth, my eye sight worse than before, the only things I could make out were 3 tall figures with green banners - they were of the Arceuus Elders. They
2	line	Key Master	muttered to each other in Archaic Language after trying to get up several times. I lost hope and stared at the sky. I had given up when the tallest of the figures bent over and brought his face right to mine and spoke
2	line	Key Master	very softly 'We can save you, but it will come at a cost'.
2	line	Player	So they saved you?
2	line	Key Master	Yes of course they saved me but look at the cost! I have horns coming out of my head and I'm still blind and stuck here... forever alone.
2	action	other
1	option	What was the curse?
2	line	Player	What was the curse?
2	line	Key Master	I have been charged to stay here to prevent the Monstrosity from escaping. Those gates and the winches that operate them are the only thing that stops it breaking free.
2	line	Player	What monstrosity? What's behind those gates?
2	line	Key Master	You really do not want to know. Leave this place human.
2	line	Player	Hey now, I'm no wimp. What's to stop me from just turning the winch to open the gate and going in?
2	line	Key Master	Me. And of course your quick demise at the mercy of Cerberus, guardian of the river of souls.
2	line	Player	But I can do it!
2	line	Key Master	You are obviously passionate at trying. But only those with great skill at slaying these types of beast may enter.
2	cond	If the player does not have hellhounds or Cerberus herself as a slayer task:
3	line	Key Master	THE VOICES! AAAHHHHH! Leave this place human!
3	action	other
2	cond	If the player has hellhounds or Cerberus herself as a slayer task:
3	line	Player	I have been charged by the slayer masters to eliminate this type of threat.
3	line	Key Master	Then you may pass... may your soul not end up consumed and forever condemned to the-
3	line	Key Master	THE VOICES! AAAHHHHH! Leave this place human!
3	action	other
1	option	Goodbye.
2	line	Player	Goodbye.
2	action	end
0	section	Reading The Journey of Souls
1	box	The book referred to an artefact being buried in Kourend, but the author did not specify where it was buried. Maybe you could persuade her to change her mind.
1	action	end
0	section	Digging for the artefact
1	box	You have found the soul bearer.
1	action	end
